/-!
# The coupling programme in one part (Parts 1-8)

Every theorem of the coupling programme, in dependency order. Each of the eight sub-parts below was
a separate module, and is copied unchanged apart from its `import` lines, inside its own `section` so
that its `open` commands stay local. Every declaration keeps its name and namespace.

| part | module | content |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `DobrushinComparison` | the arithmetic half of the W₁ Dobrushin comparison |
| 2 | `CouplingMinimality` | a discrepancy recurrence from minimality of a weighted coupling cost |
| 3 | `WassersteinComparisonBridge` | resolvent bounds, decay with a floor, finite propagation, and the measure-theoretic coupling interface |
| 4 | `FiniteCoupling` | G1 on a finite spin space |
| 5 | `CompactCoupling` | a cost-minimising coupling exists on a compact metric spin space |
| 6 | `CouplingLimit` | G1 on a compact metric spin space from finite discretisations (route 1) |
| 7 | `FiniteGluing` | gluing finite couplings; kernels close to a Dobrushin kernel |
| 8 | `QuantizedCoupling` | reference kernels obtained by quantising the continuum kernels |

Status of the mathematics: G1 is proved for finite spin spaces and
reduced, for compact ones, to discretisation hypotheses. Part 7 splits those into a reference Dobrushin kernel
plus an approximation error; Part 8 takes the reference kernels to be the quantised continuum kernels, so the
remaining hypotheses are a Dobrushin bound for the continuum single-site kernels, quantisers with small
expected displacement (they exist on every compact metric space), the approximation of the discretised heat
